::MCR_U02_L05_Quiz_Q01::
Question ID: MCR_U02_L05_Quiz_Q01
MLA Standard: MLA.MCR.AR.5
Question:
A quantity starts at 110 and grows by 5% each period. Which model represents the amount after t periods?
{
=A. A = 110(1.05)^t#Correct. A 5% increase uses growth factor 1.05.
~B. A = 110(0.05)^t#This uses the percent as the factor instead of keeping the original 100% plus 5%.
~C. A = 1.05(110)^t#This places the initial value in the exponent position.
~D. A = 110 + 5t#This is linear addition, not exponential growth.
}
